/target
models/
*.onnx
# Fixture models are stored as git-friendly ONNX protobuf TextFormat
# (`*.onnx.textproto`), which is not matched by the `*.onnx` ignore above and is
# therefore tracked. The line below documents that intent explicitly.
!**/*.onnx.textproto
# No checked-in graph fixture is exempt from the TextFormat policy. Generators
# may materialize binary ONNX files locally, but those files remain ignored.
*.safetensors
.DS_Store

# Rust
# Existing Rust entries above: /target and Cargo.lock (left as-is).
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.so
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# Squad: ignore runtime state (logs, sessions)
# Note: .squad/casting/* is identity and MUST be committed to main, not ignored
# Note: .squad/decisions/inbox/ is intentionally TRACKED (not ignored). It was
# originally grouped with runtime scratch in the 2026-07-12 "Add squad" commit on
# the assumption that drops are consumed and cleared on the same machine that wrote
# them. That assumption failed: worktrees were deleted before Scribe merged, losing
# drops that existed only locally, and with multiple machines writing concurrently a
# drop is invisible on other machines until merged. Tracking makes drops a durable
# queue that survives worktree deletion and is visible in-flight; concurrent Scribes
# add distinct files (no conflict) and delete/delete resolves cleanly on merge.
# See .squad/decisions.md — "2026-07-29 — Decision inbox is a tracked durable queue".
.squad/orchestration-log/
.squad/log/
.squad/sessions/
.squad/.scratch/
.squad/.cache/
# Squad: SubSquad activation file (local to this machine)
.squad-workstream

# Timeline written by `/profile on` when no destination is named. The curated
# samples under examples/traces/ are committed deliberately and are not this.
onnx-genai-session.perfetto.json

# Scratch files used to pass long commit messages to git commit -F.
.msg.txt
.pr-body.md
.git-msg.txt
# Belt and braces: the convention above is easy to forget, and a stray commit-
# message file has reached a PR before.
CM*.txt
PR*.md
# Extensionless variant. Removed once by 490b846c3 (as a .commitmsg/ directory)
# and re-committed as a file by #1881, because deleting the artifact left the
# name matching none of the patterns above and nothing stopped the next one.
# Root-level only, per /*.log below: it is only ever created where you run
# `git commit -F`, so a nested file of that name is somebody's, not this.
/.commitmsg
# Issue and review bodies staged the same way, for gh issue create --body-file.
.issue-*.md
# Scratch buffers used when moving a block of code between files.
.block.txt
# Test/build output teed to a file while investigating. Root-level only, so a
# fixture or a crate that legitimately tracks a .log is unaffected. Added after
# a 1364-line `cargo test` transcript reached main in #1951: the file was named
# outside every pattern above, and `git add -A` does not care what a file is
# for.
/*.log

# seq-major microbenchmark scratch crate
/bench-seqmajor/target/
bench-bins/

# Per-crate scratch written by tests at runtime (e.g. the weight-handle fixtures
# in onnx-runtime-session). Only /target is ignored above, so these nested dirs
# would otherwise be picked up by a `git add -A crates/`.
crates/*/target/

# Sebastian marlin-bench scratch: re-exported ORT-genai glm package + staging (large, reproducible)
/ort-glm-build/
/ort-glm-stage/
/ort-glm-cache/
/bench-logs/

# Roy's local benchmark scratch (see docs/benchmarks/*): raw arm dumps and
# machine-specific binary paths, never repo content.
.rg_*
.rv_*
.roy_*
# Summary transcript from roy_validate.sh. The per-gate logs match `.rv_*`,
# but the summary did not, so it was easy to commit by accident with `add -A`.
roy_validate.log

# Deckard local bench env + scratch (not for PR)
.deckard_env.sh
.scratch/

# hostlock self-test scratch (scripts/hostlock_test.sh writes these into the repo
# root deliberately -- /tmp is off-limits here -- and an aborted run leaves them)
.hostlock-selftest*
.scratch-paged/

# Leon's PR-prep scratch: PR bodies, review responses, merge-gate logs and
# mutation-battery drivers, written into a worktree root because /tmp is
# off-limits here. `.body.md` reached main this way in #2026 -- `git add -A`
# does not distinguish a dotfile at the root from repo content, and a name
# like `.body.md` looks plausible enough in `git status` to skim past.
.leon_*
.body.md
.resp*.md
.prbody*.md
# Root-anchored: these four are ordinary nouns, and a nested crate or fixture
# could reasonably want one. The scratch only ever lands in a worktree root.
/.merge.log
/.mutate*
/.suite.log
/.selftest.log
